      "problem": "Given that $‖u‖=5$ and $u\\cdot v=-30$, find the smallest possible value of $‖3v‖.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u\\cdot v| & \\le ‖u‖\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ |-30| & \\le 5\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ 6 & \\le ‖v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply both sides of the inequality by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\cdot 6 & \\le 3\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\ 18 & \\le ‖3v‖\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖3v‖$ is $18.$",
